<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean firms buy 52,500 tonnes of U.S. corn.</title>
<headline>S.Korean firms buy 52,500 tonnes of U.S. corn.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A South Korean buyer group, known as the Big Feed Mills, has bought 52,500 tonnes of U.S. corn at $126.87 a tonne, C&amp;F, from Japanese trading house Marubeni Corp, traders said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>They said the purchase was made late on Tuesday through private negotiation.</p>
<p>Shipment was slated for September 1-20 from the U.S. Gulf, with arrival due for October 20 to the western port of Inchon.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
